  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Thunderstorms this afternoon and evening are forecast for\n  southwest Montana including southern Powell, Granite, Deer \n  Lodge, and Silver Bow counties. \n\n- Thunderstorms are in the forecast through the week for much of\n  western Montana and portions of central Idaho. Storms will\n  continue in southwest Montana through the weekend. \n\nAnomalous moisture has produced cloud cover over much of the\nNorthern Rockies, which in turn has produced what we jokingly call\na cloud storm. Looking on radar we can clearly see a large area \nof higher reflectivity. Unfortunately a very dry lower atmosphere \nis only allowing for light precipitation. Valleys of northwest MT \nmay receive a trace to 0.05\" while mountainous terrain up to 0.20\"\nof precipitation today. \n\nThere is sufficient clearing of clouds that a few thunderstorms\nmay develop over southwest MT today. Any storm will be capable of\noutflow winds 35 to 45 mph, small hail, or brief heavy rain. There\nis a 5% or less chance that an isolated thunderstorm could produce\noutflow winds in excess of 58 mph.\n\nWednesday with sufficient clearing of clouds isolated\nthunderstorms may develop throughout our region. Lightning, small\nhail, and brief heavy rain being the expected threat. \n\nThe potential for afternoon thunderstorms will remain through at\nleast Friday. Saturday as the Pacific low pressure system moves\nnorth of our region, the flow flattens to a drier westerly flow\nwith decreased instability. The chances of afternoon showers and \nthunderstorms may be confined to southwest MT. Additionally, as \nthe gradient between low pressure in Canada and high pressure \nridge in the desert southwest increases, expect a breezy \nafternoon. Lakes in northwest MT may require a lake wind advisory.",
